NNOOTTEESS
       After a call to pptthhrreeaadd__sseettaaffffiinniittyy__nnpp(), the set of CPUs on which the
       thread will actually run is the intersection of the set specified in
       the _c_p_u_s_e_t argument and the set of CPUs actually present on the system.
       The system may further restrict the set of CPUs on which the thread
       runs if the "cpuset" mechanism described in ccppuusseett(7) is being used.
       These restrictions on the actual set of CPUs on which the thread will
       run are silently imposed by the kernel.

       These functions are implemented on top of the sscchheedd__sseettaaffffiinniittyy(2) and
       sscchheedd__ggeettaaffffiinniittyy(2) system calls.

       A new thread created by pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3) inherits a copy of its
       creator’s CPU affinity mask.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       In the following program, the main thread uses pptthhrreeaadd__sseettaaffffiinniittyy__nnpp()
       to set its CPU affinity mask to include CPUs 0 to 7 (which may not all
       be available on the system), and then calls pptthhrreeaadd__ggeettaaffffiinniittyy__nnpp() to
       check the resulting CPU affinity mask of the thread.

       #define _GNU_SOURCE
       #include <err.h>
       #include <pthread.h>
       #include <sched.h>
       #include <stdio.h>
       #include <stdlib.h>

       int
       main(void)
       {
           int s;
           cpu_set_t cpuset;
           pthread_t thread;

           thread = pthread_self();

           /* Set affinity mask to include CPUs 0 to 7.  */

           CPU_ZERO(&cpuset);
           for (size_t j = 0; j < 8; j++)
               CPU_SET(j, &cpuset);

           s = pthread_setaffinity_np(thread, sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
           if (s != 0)
               errc(EXIT_FAILURE, s, "pthread_setaffinity_np");

           /* Check the actual affinity mask assigned to the thread.  */

           s = pthread_getaffinity_np(thread, sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
           if (s != 0)
               errc(EXIT_FAILURE, s, "pthread_getaffinity_np");

           printf("Set returned by pthread_getaffinity_np() contained:\n");
           for (size_t j = 0; j < CPU_SETSIZE; j++)
               if (CPU_ISSET(j, &cpuset))
                   printf("    CPU %zu\n", j);

           exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);
       }

